siteconf -i [-P web] [-SB=build] [-Osite_url=...]   # writes ./configure
./configure [-DB=outdir] [-Db=reldir] [-Ovar=val]    # MY/config.mk, MY/option.mk
siteconf -g [-B outdir] [-G make]                   # Makefile, MY/Manifest.*
cd ${B} && make [goal]

MANIFEST:
    MAKE all
        NEED file1      # relative to ${a}; made as ${B}/${b}/file1
        WANT file2      # soft: resolved into MY/Manifest.all
    MAKE small
        NEED file1

In templates (TT2): D.* (config.mk), O.* (option.mk, plus O.location),
locate(...).  Keep local changes to ./configure as a patch; it is
generated deterministically.

Tests: PERL5LIB=genlib/lib:engine/lib prove -r engine/t genlib/t
